The >> operator commonly appends standard output.
Inter-process communication is commonly abbreviated IPC.
Linux IPC mechanisms include signals.
Different IPC mechanisms provide different semantics.
An Internet socket can use IPv6.
TCP provides a reliable ordered byte stream.
Binding to 0.0.0.0 generally means listening on all available IPv4 interfaces.
