Disk space should be monitored for services that write persistent data.
du estimates space used by files and directories.
Memory is a finite resource.
The kernel scheduler allocates CPU execution among runnable tasks.
Separate processes ordinarily have separate virtual address spaces.
Atomic operations can provide indivisible updates for supported operations.
Concurrency and parallelism are related but different.
A single CPU core can execute concurrent tasks through scheduling.
Virtual addresses are translated to physical memory mappings by the operating system and hardware.
Memory protection isolates address spaces.
