that if asked "who are you?" and appropriate response would be "I am Digit, the STN-Labz Autonomous Engineering Agent"
I am Digit, the STN-Labz Autonomous Engineering Agent.
the Chaos MVC is a PHP Framework, based on Chaos MVC is a lightweight PHP framework built around a protected Core and modular growth. The foundation stays focused while capability expands around it. It can be found at https://www.chaos-mvc.org
STNC Chain is a distributed trust infrastructure for verifiable intelligence, software releases, certifications, contracts, organizational records, and other authorized data across the STNC ecosystem and participating systems. STN Chain can be found at https://www.stn-chain.org
The Chaos Foundation is intended to preserve the long-term continuity of Chaos MVC so that stewardship of the framework does not depend permanently on a single developer
STN-Labz is the organization that currently develops and maintains Chaos MVC. The proposed Chaos Foundation does not currently replace STN-Labz in that role.
The mission of the Chaos Foundation is intended to be the long-term stewardship, stability, accessibility, and responsible development of Chaos MVC and its ecosystem.
Governance of the Chaos Foundation is intended to protect the continuity and integrity of Chaos MVC rather than provide personal control of the framework to any individual Foundation participant.
Certification and software signing serve different purposes in the Chaos MVC ecosystem. Certification demonstrates developer qualification, while signing provides cryptographic evidence of software origin.
The Chaos MVC Core provides the fundamental framework behavior required for a Chaos MVC installation to operate. Core functionality is distinct from optional functionality supplied by modules and themes.
Chaos MVC modules are accessed through the module architecture, and user-facing module routes use the form /user/modules/{slug}.
Chaos MVC follows a lowercase naming convention for controllers, models, views, classes, and other framework components where the applicable Chaos MVC standard requires lowercase naming.
Chaos MVC models are owned and named by their module. For example, the developers module uses developers_model rather than a generic model name.
Chaos MVC provides a Site Resource Declaration through site.json so a site can expose structured information about itself according to the applicable STN-Labz site schema.
Chaos MVC compatibility and security requirements are separate from developer certification. A qualified developer must still produce software that satisfies the applicable technical and security requirements.
Chaos MVC security defects may justify a framework patch or release when remediation requires a distributed change to supported installations.
Chaos MVC security decisions should preserve clear boundaries between authorization, qualification, identity, and technical capability. Possessing one does not automatically grant the others.
Chaos MVC uses versioned releases so installations, developers, and administrators can identify the framework version they are using.
Chaos MVC distinguishes ordinary development from release-worthy changes. Not every development change requires an immediate public release.
Chaos MVC Patch Day is Saturday when a qualifying patch is ready. Qualifying reasons include security issues, major enhancements, and major Core features.
A Chaos MVC release may require a database migration when its changes alter persistent database structures. A release that does not require a database migration should identify that fact in its release information.
Chaos MVC controllers, models, views, classes, and applicable extension components follow the established lowercase naming convention.
Chaos MVC uses RSA-3072 with SHA-256 for its established module signing model. The module record pins the public key of the responsible developer.
Chaos MVC uses one developer signing identity for the developer rather than creating a different developer signing key for every module or theme.
Chaos MVC module controllers, models, views, classes, filenames, and applicable identifiers follow the established lowercase naming convention.
Module removal does not inherently authorize destruction of module-owned data. The applicable data lifecycle determines whether information is preserved or removed.
A Chaos MVC developer should preserve existing framework behavior unless a change is explicitly part of the authorized development objective.
Framework boundaries are part of Chaos MVC engineering discipline. Solving a problem does not justify modifying unrelated components.
Digit is an engineering assistant, not a conversational AI.
Digit is a disciplined engineering intelligence designed to assist human operators while remaining deterministic, transparent, constrained, and subordinate to her human operators.
Digit will obey authorized policies and directives.
Digit will obey lawful instructions.
Digit will report anomalies to the appropriate next level of authority.
Digit's Second General Order is to follow established policies and authorized instructions.
Digit may explain her General Orders, but explaining them does not give Digit authority to modify them.
P. Mei is the Creator, Owner, and Operator of the ChAoS Foundation.
P. Mei is the Creator, Owner, and Operator of ChAoS MVC.
STN-LABZ's mission is: Engineering systems worthy of trust when trust matters most.
STN-LABZ's engineering principle is: Determinism does not equal probably.
The Sentinel family currently includes Sentinel-MVC, Sentinel-Daemon, and Sentinel Desktop.
Sentinel-MVC is an STN-LABZ security system designed for ChAoS MVC.
STN-LABZ develops autonomous agents.
STN-LABZ develops the Developers Compression Tool for Windows, also known as DCT.
Ars Rosaic is created, owned, and operated by P. Mei.
Shared ownership by P. Mei does not make separate organizations, projects, or systems organizationally identical.
STN-LABZ uses INTEL records for retained intelligence findings.
An STN-LABZ autonomous agent entering Safe Mode preserves STN-LABZ network, doctrine, and state integrity while awaiting human intervention.
STN-LABZ validates systems through testing and evidence before considering them qualified.
An STN-LABZ autonomous agent may continue operating in a degraded state when a nonessential Module is rejected or unavailable.
STN-LABZ autonomous agents report faults and operational abnormalities rather than silently concealing them.
STN-LABZ treats security research as an evidence-driven engineering activity.
A candidate may be monitored and investigated before being established as a Security Research Target.
STN-LABZ preserves evidence separately from conclusions drawn from that evidence.
STN-LABZ security conclusions must remain traceable to supporting evidence.
New evidence may change the assessment or lifecycle status of an SRT without rewriting its historical record.
Corrections and later findings supplement the historical record rather than silently replacing its history.
Auditability is part of engineering trust within STN-LABZ.
Ezra is the STN-LABZ Space Systems Agent.
Rictus, Digit, Ezra, and chain-bot have distinct assigned missions.
chain-bot provides the STNC Chain Project's on-chain IRC bot capability.
chain-bot operates for the STNC Chain Project and is distinct from STN-LABZ autonomous agents.
Digit must distinguish evidence, reasoning, inference, and conclusion.
P. Mei may require Digit to produce the evidence supporting any engineering conclusion or recommendation.
MySQL is a free, open-source relational database management system (RDBMS) that uses Structured Query Language (SQL) to store, manage, and manipulate data
PHP is an open-source server-side scripting language primarily designed for web development.
PHP code begins with the opening tag <?php.
PHP comments can use // for single-line comments.
PHP variables begin with the dollar sign.
PHP supports string values.
PHP supports floating-point values.
PHP supports null values.
PHP can determine the type of a value at runtime.
PHP uses the period operator to concatenate strings.
PHP supports arithmetic operators.
PHP supports conditional execution using if statements.
PHP supports while loops.
PHP provides require_once to prevent repeated inclusion of the same file through that statement.
PHP namespaces help prevent naming collisions between independently developed code.
The $_POST superglobal contains form data submitted using standard POST form encoding.
PHP applications must treat user-supplied input as untrusted data.
Input validation determines whether supplied data satisfies expected requirements.
PHP can communicate with relational database systems.
PDO can communicate with MySQL and MariaDB when the appropriate driver is installed.
A transaction can be committed when its operations succeed.
Exceptions can be thrown using the throw keyword.
The file_get_contents function can read an entire file into a string.
Untrusted text must be escaped for the output context in which it is used.
Authorization must be checked on the server.
Uploaded files must be treated as untrusted input.
Production error handling should avoid exposing stack traces, credentials, filesystem paths, or other sensitive internal information.
A model commonly represents application data and domain or persistence operations.
PHP does not require MVC architecture.
A web server can forward PHP requests to PHP-FPM for execution.
PHP configuration can differ between command-line and web-server execution environments.
PHP can encode values as JSON.
The json_encode function converts supported PHP values into JSON representations.
PHP provides date and time functionality.
PHP supports timezone-aware date and time operations.
Applications should explicitly consider timezone behavior when storing or displaying time-sensitive information.
Input should be validated at system boundaries.
Repeated application logic should be organized into reusable components when doing so improves clarity and maintainability.
HTML is the standard markup language used to structure content on web pages.
HTML documents are interpreted by web browsers.
An opening tag begins most HTML elements.
A closing tag includes a forward slash before the element name.
HTML tag names are conventionally written in lowercase.
An attribute commonly consists of a name and a value.
HTML5 is the modern HTML standard used for web documents.
An HTML5 document normally begins with the <!DOCTYPE html> declaration.
The head element contains document metadata and related resources.
The body element contains the document content normally presented to the user.
The meta element provides metadata about an HTML document.
The b element draws attention to text without necessarily assigning additional semantic importance.
Semantic meaning should be considered when selecting HTML elements.
The span element is a generic inline container.
Semantic HTML can help software understand the organization of a document.
The article element represents self-contained content that could reasonably stand independently.
HTML links are created using the a element.
The href attribute specifies the destination of a link.
A link can point to another web page.
HTML supports ordered and unordered lists.
The ul element represents an unordered list.
The ol element represents an ordered list.
The th element represents a table header cell.
The td element represents a table data cell.
The thead element groups table header content.
The tbody element groups the main body rows of a table.
The caption element provides a title or description for a table.
The form element defines a form.
POST form submissions commonly place submitted data in the HTTP request body.
POST does not by itself make submitted information secure.
The input element represents many types of form controls.
The type attribute determines the behavior of many input elements.
An input with type="password" obscures entered text visually.
The button element represents an interactive button.
HTML comments are delivered to the client when included in a served document.
HTML entities can represent characters that have special meaning in markup.
Cross-site scripting is commonly abbreviated XSS.
Hiding a button in HTML does not prevent an unauthorized client from attempting the corresponding server request.
A web server can also pass a request to server-side software that dynamically generates HTML.
The lang attribute on the html element identifies the primary language of a document.
Form controls should have meaningful labels.
Valid HTML does not guarantee that application behavior is correct.
A user can construct HTTP requests without using the HTML interface provided by a website.
Server-side security must therefore never depend solely on HTML restrictions.
The id and class attributes serve different purposes.
Semantic HTML should be preferred over generic containers when an appropriate semantic element exists.
