C source code is translated into executable machine code by a compiler and related build tools.
A C implementation consists of a compiler and supporting implementation facilities.
A C program begins execution through the main function in a hosted environment.
An identifier cannot begin with a digit.
A variable definition allocates storage for an object unless language rules specify otherwise.
