A non-repeatable read occurs when repeated reads can observe a changed committed value.
Serialization anomalies involve concurrent executions producing outcomes inconsistent with required serializable behavior.
A database can use predicate, range, metadata, or other lock forms depending on implementation.
Database systems can detect and resolve deadlocks by aborting a transaction.
